{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01YXGDY7N2ZPBazVL2bmH3Pa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GwqNDVsm89zZwHKopxRg4Q","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","old_string":"- **AttacksTriggeredEvent is never fired** by the engine (combat.py). sos_1's\n  attack trigger (and fdn_194 Etali) depend on it. Added a single `fire_event`\n  in `declare_attackers_step` for each declared attacker, populating\n  `creature=` and `attacker=`. Additive, mirrors how other turn-based events fire.","new_string":"- **AttacksTriggeredEvent is never fired** by the engine (combat.py). sos_1's\n  attack trigger (and fdn_194 Etali) depend on it. Added a single `fire_event`\n  in `declare_attackers_step` for each declared attacker, populating\n  `creature=` and `attacker=`. Additive, mirrors how other turn-based events fire.\n\n- **sos_1 \"exile instead of graveyard\":** the spell cast from the graveyard\n  moves STACK→GRAVEYARD in `_resolve_spell`, a path that does not consult\n  replacement effects (only battlefield-leaving moves do). Rather than rework\n  the replacement subsystem, used a single card-local flag\n  `_exile_instead_of_graveyard` read at that one point in `_resolve_spell`\n  (deviates from TODO's suggested ReplacementEffect, which would not fire here).\n  Observable behavior (spell ends in exile) is identical.\n\n- **sos_1 \"may cast target\":** modeled the \"may\" as part of target choice —\n  one legal target auto-casts (per TODO \"auto-select instead of prompting\");\n  with 2+, `choose_card` picks one or returns None to decline. No separate\n  yes/no prompt."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":249,"cache_read_input_tokens":242017,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":249},"output_tokens":10,"service_tie